node_modules
# `dist` is COMMITTED as of RA1 and deliberately not ignored.
#
# `thruline ui` embeds it into the binary (crates/cli/build.rs), so a checkout
# with no npm in it must still be able to build a working product. That is the
# whole point of the command.
#
# It is safe to commit and the safety is structural: vite.config.js switches
# publicDir off for `vite build` and copies only the `fonts` allowlist, so dist
# carries no `fixtures/` and therefore no transcript content. Verified at RA1 by
# scanning the tree for absolute home paths (none) — 236 KB, 10 files.
#
# THE OBLIGATION THAT COMES WITH IT: any session that changes `ui/src` must run
# `cd ui && npm run build` and commit the result, or the binary ships a UI older
# than the source and nothing will say so.
.DS_Store
public/fixtures/local.json
public/fixtures/index.json
public/fixtures/projects/
public/fixtures/project.json

# F01: `dist` is committed, `dist/fixtures/` never is.
#
# The safety above is structural — `vite build` copies only the `fonts`
# allowlist — but the guarantee covers what the BUILD writes, not what a
# process later drops into the tree. A 351 MB export of real transcript content
# was once copied into `dist/fixtures/` after a build, untracked and unignored,
# one `git add -A` away from being published. This line is the belt to that
# structural brace: an export under `dist` is never committable.
dist/fixtures/
